### Cancel a transfer with AbortController via abortSignal

Source: https://github.com/aws/aws-sdk-js-v3/blob/main/preview/lib-transfer-manager/README.md

Pass a standard AbortController signal through transferOptions.abortSignal to cancel a transfer. An aborted transfer throws an error with name "AbortError".

```javascript
const controller = new AbortController();
const timeoutId = setTimeout(() => controller.abort(), 30_000);

try {
  const download = await tm.download({ Bucket: "source-bucket", Key: "some-key" }, { abortSignal: controller.signal });
  const data = await download.Body?.transformToByteArray();
  console.log(`Downloaded ${data.byteLength} bytes`);
} catch (error) {
  if (error.name === "AbortError") {
    console.log("Download aborted");
  } else {
    throw error;
  }
} finally {
  clearTimeout(timeoutId);
}
```

